{
  "schema": "ld-s10y-image/figure-spec@2",
  "id": "fig-choice-n36-rays-FIRST",
  "mode": "deterministic",
  "description": "One four-candidate panel for jointly recognizing the original ray f and its converse g, including unbounded continuation and endpoint inclusion. The candidates are schematic additions, not a recovered textbook image.",
  "source": {
    "authoritativeText": [
      {
        "lesson": "alg8-c6-s1-n36",
        "exercise": "731",
        "text": "731。 作出由公式$y=2x+3$（$x\\in[0,\\ +\\infty[$）给出的函数 $f$ 的图象.用方程给出函数 $f$ 的相反关系 $g$。 指出关系 $g$ 的定义域和值域。 作出关系 $g$ 的图象。"
      }
    ],
    "authoredBasis": "Independent derivation from the complete written exercise: f={(x,2x+3):x>=0} is the closed ray starting at (0,3); swapping coordinates gives g={(x,(x-3)/2):x>=3}, a closed ray starting at (3,0), D_g=[3,+infinity), R_g=[0,+infinity). Candidate A is f: (0,3),(1,5),(3,9), closed start, upper-right arrow. Candidate C is g: (3,0),(5,1),(9,3), closed start, upper-right arrow. Candidate B deliberately removes the original restriction after swapping: the entire line y=(x-3)/2, through (-1,-2),(3,0),(9,3), with arrows in both directions, D=R=real numbers. Candidate D deliberately replaces x>=0 by x>0: the f-supporting ray with an open endpoint (0,3), so D=(0,+infinity), R=(3,+infinity). These are distinct deliberately authored alternatives, not source pixels. All panels have equal x/y unit length 24 pixels; A/B origins are (60,560)/(370,560), C/D origins (60,130)/(370,130) in the renderer's upward-y coordinates. Each panel displays x=-1..9 and y=-3..10; arrows indicate continuation beyond the drawn window, never finite domains. Light grids, axis labels, unit ticks, panel letters, visible (1,5)/(5,1) sample points and coordinate labels are explicitly modern schematic additions. A/C correspond by exchanging (0,3)<->(3,0), (1,5)<->(5,1) and all points on their rays.",
    "inventory": [
      {
        "id": "candidate-A",
        "description": "Correct f ray, closed endpoint and one-way continuation. Coordinates are translated/scaled modern additions to the written relationship.",
        "objects": ["A-start-marker","A-sample-marker","A-ray"],
        "assertions": ["A-visible-rise-run","A-rise-run","A-tip-relation","A-collinear","A-arrow"],
        "requires": ["pointRelationships"]
      },
      {
        "id": "candidate-B",
        "description": "Deliberate unrestricted converse-line alternative with both directions extending without bound; the marked (3,0) is an interior point, not an endpoint.",
        "objects": ["B-cross-marker","B-sample-marker","B-backward","B-forward"],
        "assertions": ["B-visible-rise-run","B-low-relation","B-sample-relation","B-tip-relation","B-collinear","B-back-arrow","B-forward-arrow"],
        "requires": ["pointRelationships"]
      },
      {
        "id": "candidate-C",
        "description": "Correct g closed ray; ordered pairs swap those on f, and its starting abscissa is 3.",
        "objects": ["C-start-marker","C-sample-marker","C-ray"],
        "assertions": ["C-visible-rise-run","C-rise-run","C-tip-relation","C-collinear","C-arrow"],
        "requires": ["pointRelationships"]
      },
      {
        "id": "candidate-D",
        "description": "Deliberate endpoint-exclusion alternative: same supporting ray as f, open (0,3), with one unbounded direction.",
        "objects": ["D-start-marker","D-sample-marker","D-ray"],
        "assertions": ["D-visible-rise-run","D-rise-run","D-tip-relation","D-collinear","D-arrow"],
        "requires": ["pointRelationships"]
      },
      {
        "id": "modern-equal-unit-grids",
        "description": "Four finite 10-column by 13-row display windows; their bounds are visual windows only, not graph domains.",
        "objects": ["A-grid","B-grid","C-grid","D-grid"],
        "assertions": ["A-grid-dimensions","B-grid-dimensions","C-grid-dimensions","D-grid-dimensions"],
        "requires": ["gridDimensions"]
      }
    ]
  },
  "canvas": {"width":640,"height":880,"boundingBox":[0,880,640,0],"background":"paper","keepAspectRatio":true},
  "display": {"layout":"scroll","purpose":"instructional","minTextPx":16,"widths":[640]},
  "layout": {"minLabelGap":4},
